msgid "timeline.copy.substantial_rehab_explained"
msgstr "A substantial rehabilitation involves major reconstruction of a building, including replacement of most of its major systems. When a building is substantially rehabilitated, its apartments can become permanently exempt from rent stabilization because the building is treated as newly constructed. If you do not believe a substantial rehabilitation occurred, there is a chance your apartment was improperly destabilized."

