#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/content/GceRentIncreaseLimitsContent.tsx:33
msgid "If you are offered a new lease after {0}, then your landlord can’t raise your apartment’s monthly rent higher than:"
msgstr "If you are offered a new lease after {0}, then your landlord can’t raise your apartment’s monthly rent higher than:"

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/content/RsLeaseRenewalContent.tsx:10
msgid "If you are rent-stabilized your landlord cannot simply decide they don’t want you as a tenant anymore, they are limited to certain reasons for evicting you."
msgstr "If you are rent-stabilized your landlord cannot simply decide they don’t want you as a tenant anymore, they are limited to certain reasons for evicting you."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/content/RsSuccessionContent.tsx:10
msgid "If you are the immediate family member of a rent-stabilized tenant and have been living with them immediately prior to their moving or passing away, you might be entitled to take over the lease."
msgstr "If you are the immediate family member of a rent-stabilized tenant and have been living with them immediately prior to their moving or passing away, you might be entitled to take over the lease."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrDhcrComplaintContent.tsx:21
msgid "If you believe you’ve been charged more than the legal rent for your apartment, you may be able to file an overcharge complaint with DHCR. DHCR can review the evidence, determine whether an overcharge occurred, and order an appropriate remedy when it finds a violation."
msgstr "If you believe you’ve been charged more than the legal rent for your apartment, you may be able to file an overcharge complaint with DHCR. DHCR can review the evidence, determine whether an overcharge occurred, and order an appropriate remedy when it finds a violation."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/assertYourRightsSections.tsx:69
msgid "If you believe your landlord has violated your rights, you may be able to take formal action."
msgstr "If you believe your landlord has violated your rights, you may be able to take formal action."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrWithholdRentContent.tsx:29
msgid "If you choose to withhold rent, consider setting your monthly rent money aside while you withhold. If a court later determines that you owe some or all of the withheld rent, having the money available can be important."
msgstr "If you choose to withhold rent, consider setting your monthly rent money aside while you withhold. If a court later determines that you owe some or all of the withheld rent, having the money available can be important."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrWithholdRentContent.tsx:26
msgid "If you decide to withhold rent"
msgstr "If you decide to withhold rent"

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/content/RsStabilizedLeaseContent.tsx:73
msgid "If you don’t have a lease, or your lease doesn’t say that your apartment is rent stabilized, you may still have the rights and protections that come with rent stabilization."
msgstr "If you don’t have a lease, or your lease doesn’t say that your apartment is rent stabilized, you may still have the rights and protections that come with rent stabilization."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/assertYourRightsSections.tsx:99
msgid "If you live in a rent stabilized apartment, there are additional programs you can use to try to reduce or limit your rent."
msgstr "If you live in a rent stabilized apartment, there are additional programs you can use to try to reduce or limit your rent."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/knowYourRightsSections.tsx:45
msgid "If you live in a rent-stabilized apartment, or think your apartment should be rent stabilized, you may have additional protections around your rent and ability to remain in your home."
msgstr "If you live in a rent-stabilized apartment, or think your apartment should be rent stabilized, you may have additional protections around your rent and ability to remain in your home."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrRentReductionCheckContent.tsx:14
msgid "If you’re concerned about your rent, finding out whether there is an existing order can give you important context before you decide what to do."
msgstr "If you’re concerned about your rent, finding out whether there is an existing order can give you important context before you decide what to do."

#: src/Components/Pages/Landing/Landing.tsx:31
msgid "If your apartment is rent stabilized, or has ever been rent stabilized, you should have a rent history document."
msgstr "If your apartment is rent stabilized, or has ever been rent stabilized, you should have a rent history document."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/content/RsStabilizedLeaseContent.tsx:18
msgid "If your apartment is rent stabilized, your landlord must give you a rent-stabilized lease. Your lease should tell you that your apartment is rent stabilized and provide information about your rent and the terms of your tenancy."
msgstr "If your apartment is rent stabilized, your landlord must give you a rent-stabilized lease. Your lease should tell you that your apartment is rent stabilized and provide information about your rent and the terms of your tenancy."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrAskLandlordContent.tsx:72
msgid "If your concern involves something that happened before your landlord became the owner, don’t assume that you have no recourse simply because the current owner wasn’t involved at the time."
msgstr "If your concern involves something that happened before your landlord became the owner, don’t assume that you have no recourse simply because the current owner wasn’t involved at the time."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/knowYourRightsSections.tsx:52
msgid "If your lease looks <0>something like this</0>, then your apartment is very likely rent stabilized. But even if your lease does not look like that, you may still be rent stabilized."
msgstr "If your lease looks <0>something like this</0>, then your apartment is very likely rent stabilized. But even if your lease does not look like that, you may still be rent stabilized."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/AssertYourRights/content/AyrNeighborsContent.tsx:40
msgid "If your neighbors are facing similar problems, you can work together to document what is happening, raise concerns with your landlord, contact government agencies, or take action as a group. When tenants come together, you have power."
msgstr "If your neighbors are facing similar problems, you can work together to document what is happening, raise concerns with your landlord, contact government agencies, or take action as a group. When tenants come together, you have power."

#: src/Components/Pages/RightsPages/KnowYourRights/content/NychaGrieveContent.tsx:10
msgid "In instances where residents disagree with management decisions or believe their rights have been violated, they have the right to grieve these issues through a formal process. Residents can file grievances online through the resident portal or on paper by visiting the management office."
msgstr "In instances where residents disagree with management decisions or believe their rights have been violated, they have the right to grieve these issues through a formal process. Residents can file grievances online through the resident portal or on paper by visiting the management office."

